# Positions on lines holding non-ASCII text. On line 9 the `data`
# argument starts at UTF-16 column 34 and at byte offset 39 of the line:
# if the server confused the two it would answer about the `%d` instead,
# which is the classic language-server bug.
request 1 initialize {}
notify initialized {}
open file:///unicode.v verilog unicode.v

# Hover and go-to-definition on the `data` after the string literal.
ask 2 textDocument/hover file:///unicode.v 9 34
ask 3 textDocument/definition file:///unicode.v 9 34

# The same `data`, but at the byte offset instead of the UTF-16 column:
# that lands inside the string, which is not a name.
ask 4 textDocument/definition file:///unicode.v 9 39

# Renaming rewrites the occurrence on the non-ASCII line at the right
# column.
ask 5 textDocument/rename file:///unicode.v 4 20 {"newName":"payload"}

request 6 shutdown null
notify exit
